# cyto-jelly — heart's fast clock + self-restart, lateralised into a directional swimmer.
# = cyto-heart.gene (relaxation-oscillator clock on rr->rg->rb, contract on the rg phase, oriented division,
#   repair, self-restart) PLUS the jellyfish morphogen machinery: a seeded bb organizer sources a gb gradient,
#   division is asymmetric+oriented (Mitosis bb across gb) -> a 2D sheet with an off-centre organizer, and the
#   contraction is gated on (clock phase) AND (high-gb flank) so ONE side pulses at clock speed -> directional
#   bend -> thrust.  Bond types used: rr, rg, rb, gb, bb = 5 (the GENOME_MAX_BOND_TYPES cap).
# Seed the founder with the organizer mark: sandbox -Dsandboxseed=bb:200,r:500 (bb = maternal determinant).

# grow biomass
Break rr : Biomass < 4000 : Convert rr @15
Light : rr < 8000 & rg < 1000 : FormBond r r
# clock ring  rr -> rg -> rb -> rr  (heart's relaxation oscillator)
Break rb : rg < rb & rg < 1000 : FormBond r r @7
Break rr : rb < rr & rb < 1000 : FormBond r g @7
Break rg : rr < rg & rr < 1000 : FormBond r b @7
# organizer: seeded bb persists on its own (never metabolised -> intracellular, allocated whole on division),
# so NO self-sustain gene needed — keeps the light budget lean for the clock.
# morphogen: organizer sources gb (break-powered, NOT light, so the clock keeps full light); everyone sinks it.
Light : bb > 0 & rg > 1000 : FormBond g b
Break gb : Conc(gb) > 30 : Convert gb
# DIRECTIONAL locomotion: contract on the clock's rg-phase AND only on the high-gb flank (fast + one-sided)
Break rg : rr < rg & rr < 1000 & rg > 6000 & Conc(gb) > 20 : Contract @15
# oriented + asymmetric division -> 2D sheet, organizer kept off-centre (lateralised gradient)
Break rg : rr < rg & rr < 1000 & rg > 21500 : Mitosis bb across gb @15
# cohesion + self-restart (kick a stalled clock when all three phases coexist)
Break rr : rb < rr & rb < 1000 : Repair @15
Break rb : rr > 999 & rg > 999 & rb > 999 : FormBond r r
